From 7e89e4365fd36ca006670788ec2c1527bfd0c61c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Zimmermann <tzimmermann@suse.de>
Date: Mon, 30 Sep 2024 15:03:22 +0200
Subject: drm/vc4: Use video aperture helpers
Git-commit: 7e89e4365fd36ca006670788ec2c1527bfd0c61c
Patch-mainline: v6.13-rc1
References: stable-fixes

DRM's aperture functions have long been implemented as helpers
under drivers/video/ for use with fbdev. Avoid the DRM wrappers by
calling the video functions directly.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Zimmermann <tzimmermann@suse.de>
Cc: Maxime Ripard <mripard@kernel.org>
Cc: Dave Stevenson <dave.stevenson@raspberrypi.com>
Cc: Raspberry Pi Kernel Maintenance <kernel-list@raspberrypi.com>
Acked-by: Javier Martinez Canillas <javierm@redhat.com>
Acked-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
Link: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20240930130921.689876-25-tzimmermann@suse.de
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
  * driver.
  */
 
+#include <linux/aperture.h>
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/component.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
@@ -30,7 +31,6 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 
-#include <drm/drm_aperture.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fbdev_dma.h>
@@ -356,7 +356,7 @@ static int vc4_drm_bind(struct device *d
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = drm_aperture_remove_framebuffers(driver);
+	ret = aperture_remove_all_conflicting_devices(driver->name);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
 
